A||N||18||bHooper||the Good, the Bad, and the Ugly!||||1||
Z||000000||bHooper||06-08-2001||05:33 PM||||you decide which is which.<P>on this day, june 8th, i sat out to work on my "new" SE.  it needed the bloddy rear manifold exchanged.  i picked up the appropriate studs from Saturn, and came home to start working on the car around noon.<P>dismantlying everything to drop the cradle, went just as planned... narry a hitch, until i noticed that the inside passenger shock tower stud (the one that the grill rest on) was spinning, not the nut.  upon further investigation, i found that this stud was completely loose on the strut top plate.  perhaps this is the source of the wiggle that this car has in long fast right hand bends in the road!?<P>that was the good.<P>next, i started working on the manifold, shearing off a bolt from the crossover... not a big deal, that can be welded up later.  on the next bolt (the dreaded lower one), the head rounds off, and i am left with grinding and drilling as my only options!  the manifold itself has a 1/32-1/16" crack in it.  after deliberating ofer this a bit, i decided to patch it up with Permatex Ultra Copper gasket material, long enough so i can get the bugger inspected next week.<P>that was the bad....<P>and now for the UGLY!<P>as i went to grab the jack (from underneath the 4x4), but what did i notice under the drivers side door?!  thats right... a nice big wet spot!  Damnit!  I opened a hole in the cooling tube!  <B>Aghhhh!!!</B>  right at the bracket.  <P>man i'm sick.... whats worse is that this is my airconditioned car, and the salvage yard was supposed to crush the remainder of the 2 cars this week!<P>what a really really bad day!  i think i'm gonna go crawl back under my blankie!<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT 5 speed<BR>*Black '86 SE Automatic||||reg||1
Z||000001||stimpy||06-08-2001||07:18 PM||||All I can say is, aww man, that sucks.||||reg||1
Z||000002||flyntus||06-08-2001||07:34 PM||||That's what I call buzzard luck.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Songman||06-09-2001||07:02 PM||||Okay...so what did you do about it?<P>I did mine today so now I have to fix it too! With mine it couldn't be helped. Damn rusty jack point caved in! <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||9
Z||000004||bHooper||06-09-2001||07:38 PM||||Well, with the help of Bob Englert (without home i wouldn't have been able to do this in one day!), we went to the salvage yard and yanked 3 cooling tubes (1 driver and 2 passenger), front control arms (for Bob's Northern Nightmare), and came home.<P>We pulled the rack (braking one tie rod bolt), removed the old tube and installed the new one.  Removed a good tie rod end off of the salvaged rack and installed the rack.  <P>After that, Bob left and I filled the car up with coolant.<P><B>However</B> I heard a pouring sound from underneath the car.... damn!  BUSTED coolant hose from the water pump!  I must have ripped it when I tilted the cradle back.<P>At that point, I called it an evening and will put the thing back together on monday.<P>As for the manifold... i have "salved" it in parmatex ultra copper, in hopes that that will get me through inspection!<P><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT 5 speed<BR>*Black '86 SE Automatic||||reg||1
Z||000005||Formula88||06-09-2001||08:41 PM||||Good luck with her, Hoop.  I feel your pain.  Still, she's a sweet SE.  It'll be worth the hassle when it's done.||||reg||6
Z||000006||Bob Englert||06-09-2001||08:54 PM||||Hoop:<P>I like the sound of it - "Northern Nightmare"<P>I did get the driver side control arm out when I got home by grinding the head off the rear control arm bolt.  I also got the spring out of the passenger side and the front lower control arm bolt.  <P>The rear bolt is frozen solid to the inner sleeve of the bushing just like it was on the driver's side.  Tried heating the bolt head, beating the hell out of it with a chisel, and beating on the bolt itself.  It isn't moving at all.  Looks like it will be saw and/or grinder time again for that one too.  I still can't believe we got the spindles, springs, and all 4 control arms out of the silver SE in about 1 1/2 hours.  IT is taking me more than 1 hour per bolt on the maroon car.<P>Anyway, happy to help, sorry about the hose.  Hopefully it is all routine from here.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000007||bHooper||06-09-2001||09:18 PM||||oooooh... not fun, Bob.  I just hope I don't rund into those same surprises when I start the suspension work on the black car (whenever that will be).<P>thanks for the compliment, '88!  shes a nice ride (especially for the price), but does need a few things here and there, to be perfect.  Like getting rid of those drop spindles, and ST rear springs, and replaceing them with some Eibach's.  I really want to haver her set up like the Red car (only with rubber bushings in the front so it doesn't squeak!)<P><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT 5 speed<BR>*Black '86 SE Automatic||||reg||1
Z||000008||Songman||06-09-2001||09:19 PM||||So you gotta take the front end apart to change the tubes?<P>Wanna sell the drivers side one or is that the one you used? <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Toddster||06-09-2001||09:30 PM||||Wait...can you hear it? The theme music from the movie... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000010||Galen||06-09-2001||10:05 PM||||see now, all ya had to do was drive down here and I would have given you a couple free..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Galen - 1988 Hawaiian Orchid Coupe Auto 4Banger - <A HREF="http://myfiero.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero Website</A><BR>AIM: WookieeNC||||reg||1
Z||000011||Bob Englert||06-10-2001||12:08 AM||||Songman:<P>In my experience there is no way to remove the drivers side pipe without first removing the steering rack from the car.  You also have to bend the front left brake line over the end of the tube before you can swing it out of the way.  As long as your rack mounting screws are not rusted to the frame, the rack actually comes out very easily.  <P>The passenger side tube is a piece of cake compared to the driver's side, nothing really needed to take apart for the right side.<P>We did remove the spare tire tube to get easy access to the rack bolts and the cooling tube mounting bolt.<P>Like most Fiero repairs, it is pretty easy after you have done it a couple of times.<P><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000012||Songman||06-10-2001||01:51 AM||||I'm thinking I see a length of rubber hose in my future. When I get ready to redo the car, then I will go to all of that trouble.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000013||bHooper||06-10-2001||08:21 AM||||songman, you could try the Leakfinder 2000 stuff, as seen on TV :d<P>It is a PITA, and, as Bob said, there is not apparent way to do it without removing the rack or haveing the car 9 feet in the air (not many of us have our own personal lifts, either).<P><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT 5 speed<BR>*Black '86 SE Automatic||||reg||1
Z||000014||FieroHarry||06-10-2001||09:12 AM||||Bob,<BR>"Northern Nightmare"? is Hoop refering to that GT you bought last summer?<P>------------------<BR><B>Harry Waggoner</B><BR>1985 GT 264K+ <I>FOCOSEVA,FOCOA</I><BR><B>"Im not driving to fast, Im flying to low!"</B>||||reg||5
Z||000015||Songman||06-10-2001||01:16 PM||||I don't know if this will actually work or not..<P>I was looking through a Haynes manual (maybe Chilton's) this morning and they said that you can just remove the front wheel on the side you are workin on and swing the tube way out almost 90 degrees to the side of the car and snake it out without taking the rack out.<P>Good thing I have a parts car to try it on. Yeah, I got a parts car! I am usually just to lazy to take stuff off of it. It is easier just to buy something someone else already has off! hehe<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000016||Bob Englert||06-10-2001||03:17 PM||||Songman:<P>The Haynes manual is wrong!  The instructions are that simple for the passenger side but the steering column and left front brake line prevents you from doing that on the drivers side.<P>It was frustrating as hell the first time I did the drivers side.  The manual said it was so easy and I couldn't get the pipe out to save my life.  I ended up taking a hacksaw to the old pipe but that didn't help me when putting in the new one.  The rack does have to come out.<P>The good news is you don't really need to have the car high in the air to replace them.  <P>Harry: <BR>"Northern Nightmare" is the maroon 87 GT I bought last fall from the local Pontiac dealer before it went to auction.  It was a Michigan car that was driven down and traded in here.  The previous owner spent all his money on detailing and interior trim (new switches, etc.) and nothing on mechanical repairs.  The car needs a new clutch, had no rear brakes, several sensors were not working, A/C was converted and is not working, and the front suspension was shot.  I just got the last lower control arm bolt out today by grinding off the head of the bolt.  The car is definitely worth saving but it is fighting me hard!<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000017||Songman||06-10-2001||08:00 PM||||Just my luck... I knew it looked awfully tight in there when I had it up on the lift yesterday...<P>I'm just gonna go tomorrow and cut the crushed section out and put a hose in. I think that will be the easiest and best thing for right now. <P>Thanks.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000018||007DOUG||06-11-2001||11:01 AM||||First you removed the tint, now you're breaking coolant lines. And whats this talk about removing the drop spindles.<P>Don't make me come down there and take the SE back "home". <P>------------------<BR>4 Indy pace Cars<BR>84 T-top<BR>2 86 Red GTs (twins) <BR>86 GT Yellow ASAP<BR>86 GT Blue w/4:10 tranny<BR>86 GT Pearl White 3.4 T-top<BR>88 Faded red Formula 5 speed<BR>2 Black 88 GT's (twins)<P>However......<BR><I>"Time is my most precious and most perishable of all my possessions."</I>||||reg||12
